Advanced synchronous-machine excitation and frequency study (@pe-machine-control-study: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electrical-power-engineering, #source "../sources/Power-System-Dynamics-and-Control-Kulkarni.lingua#r_2T4WS3TCPCXRB5JEH7HTN5FAHQ", #source "../sources/Electric-Machines-MIT-6-685.lingua#r_6A4HM4XV13NAZDRV92PZDJ31XH", #source "../sources/Excitation-Systems-Hydroelectric-FIST-2026.lingua#r_725R40RX14YMRTQNWKGHY12JCN", #source "../sources/ANDES-Modeling-and-Analysis-Manual.lingua#r_5JM9DVGXWSD8645484SZP5XRSZ", #electrical-power-engineering "../study/An-integrated-electrical-power-system-investigation.lingua#r_06BN864FF9C0AN3EWZJE78Y6Y3") { r_15649BSJNFYXQJY9YYPS208JZY
**Read:** [Power System Dynamics and Control — A. M. Kulkarni](../sources/Power-System-Dynamics-and-Control-Kulkarni.lingua#r_2T4WS3TCPCXRB5JEH7HTN5FAHQ), entire programme and substantial exercises; [Electric Machines — MIT 6.685, Fall 2013](../sources/Electric-Machines-MIT-6-685.lingua#r_6A4HM4XV13NAZDRV92PZDJ31XH), complete relevant synchronous/control models; [Excitation Systems for Hydroelectric Units — FIST 3-14](../sources/Excitation-Systems-Hydroelectric-FIST-2026.lingua#r_725R40RX14YMRTQNWKGHY12JCN), entire applicable manual; [ANDES — dynamic modelling and analysis manual](../sources/ANDES-Modeling-and-Analysis-Manual.lingua#r_5JM9DVGXWSD8645484SZP5XRSZ), whole relevant model/eigenvalue/time-domain and initialization methods.

Complete all of [Power System Dynamics and Control — A. M. Kulkarni](../sources/Power-System-Dynamics-and-Control-Kulkarni.lingua#r_2T4WS3TCPCXRB5JEH7HTN5FAHQ), the full dynamic machine/control notes in [Electric Machines — MIT 6.685, Fall 2013](../sources/Electric-Machines-MIT-6-685.lingua#r_6A4HM4XV13NAZDRV92PZDJ31XH) and the whole applicable [Excitation Systems for Hydroelectric Units — FIST 3-14](../sources/Excitation-Systems-Hydroelectric-FIST-2026.lingua#r_725R40RX14YMRTQNWKGHY12JCN) manual. Choose a single/multimachine system with explicit bases, source energy, excitation, governor, load and network state.

Reconstruct dq/state/terminal equations, consistent initialization and reduced models. Compare frequency, rotor-angle, terminal-voltage and reactive responses as distinct observables. Derive and verify local modes, then test a large disturbance with actual control/field/current/rate limits. Trace mechanical/auxiliary energy and cooling constraints rather than treating a requested power change as always available.

Use independent analytical limits, Jacobian checks, time-step refinement and suitable measurement or a complete documented case. Change an operating point or controller parameter and predict a response not used in fitting. Explain model discrepancy and which reduction is appropriate for the time scale. The final account should link graduate dynamic reasoning to actual equipment, sensing, settings, tests and continuing operation, with a clear distinction between a locally stable linearization and a demonstrated large-disturbance recovery.

**Continue:** [An integrated electrical-power-system investigation](../study/An-integrated-electrical-power-system-investigation.lingua#r_06BN864FF9C0AN3EWZJE78Y6Y3).

**Return:** [Electrical power engineering — sources, networks, machines and continuing service](../Electrical-power-engineering.lingua#r_300EPNGATK7PHWNZCQFBXGZFCQ).
